WEBVTT

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:13.175
A quadratic equation includes a squared variable and can have two solutions. First

00:00:13.175 --> 00:00:17.218
identify a, b, and c in standard form.

00:00:20.018 --> 00:00:26.786
The quadratic formula uses these three values to calculate the solutions.

00:00:29.586 --> 00:00:38.001
For x squared minus five x plus six equals zero, the solutions are two and three.

00:00:38.001 --> 00:00:43.818
Substituting either value makes the equation equal zero.
